  "metric_definitions": {
    "navigation_success": "A recorded finish after this one goal AND final goal errors; duration_completed is not success. Physical collision invalidates success.",
    "base_motion": "Measured Plant x/y/yaw and path sums, not base_anchor_error_m. Side=absolute world y for the shared x-axis goal. Full-run metrics include post-finish standby, which is separately reported.",
    "timing": "Plant origin=1000+result.simulated_s-result.elapsed_s; navigation event ros_time is aligned to that origin. Goal-finish uses their actual ROS timestamps. Header receipt time=runner.start_ros_time+header-record elapsed_s, not header[3].",
    "phase": "Time-weighted left-sample mean over positive-start progress messages from goal to finish (or plant stop without finish). Zero scale includes real pauses/cancellation aftermath; gaps remain in the observed interval.",
    "cycles": "p95 uses linear interpolation of all status cycle_ms during the navigation window; successful native-reference delivery p95 is also given. Native controller has no MPPI cycle metric. Post-finish standby is excluded.",
    "faults": "True-message count and false-to-true episode count on /tracking_fault after goal; repeated True publications are one continuous episode until False.",
    "snapshot_audit": "Nearest recorder header received no later than each status. Separate subscriber scheduling means it is contextual evidence, not necessarily the exact object captured at solve start; candidate_min_gap is from the actual cycle diagnostic.",
    "comparability": "Same navigation goal [0.45,0,0], uncertainty scale 1, position-servo Plant, current native planner/controller and physical limits. MPPI arm-enabled mode versus native tracker+joint bridge. One seed/run per condition; not a statistical robustness result."
  },
  "conclusions": [
    "Empty native and empty MPPI both emitted goal finish. Dynamic native collided at 8.365 s. Dynamic MPPI stopped around x=0.0603 m, stayed collision-free for 24 s, and did not finish. Dynamic navigation with arm avoidance has not passed.",
    "Dynamic MPPI first stopped issuing nonzero base commands around 1.58 s because native_progress_slowed_during_plan rejected delivery while original controller phase scale was falling. The obstacle appears at 2 s. It later reported no_feasible_candidate with a usable dynamic snapshot, then snapshot aging during native replanning, then native trajectory cancellation. The early stop is not evidence of successful dynamic avoidance.",
    "MPPI navigation deliveries were nominal only in the four main runs; these logs do not demonstrate successful arm_only obstacle avoidance.",
    "The separate scene_audit witness prescribes retraction while replaying a recorded base path; it supports sampled geometric feasibility only and is not an MPPI/ROS result."
